BLOCKER ANALYSIS (honest, evidenced — Honesty Covenant #1 "no red-as-green")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The whole-app build does not compile in THIS checkout because of two PRE-EXISTING
defects in files this unit never touches. Proven by building the UNMODIFIED tree
(my 9 new files moved aside, TeslaSyncApp.swift + Localizable.xcstrings reverted to
HEAD, xcodegen regenerated): the baseline build ALSO fails, BASELINE_BUILD_EXIT=65.

  1) Hard compile error (pre-existing, non-Admin):
     TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/AISuggestNewGeofences.swift:129:22:
       error: escaping closure captures non-escaping parameter 'content'

  2) Swift compiler IRGen crash (pre-existing toolchain bug, non-Admin):
     While evaluating IRGenRequest for TeslaSync/feature-views/AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift
     While emitting IR SIL function "@$sSbScA_pSgIeAghyg_SbIeAghn_TR"
       = reabstraction thunk helper from
         @escaping @isolated(any) @Sendable (Bool, Actor?) -> ()  to  (Bool) -> ()
       llvm::report_fatal_error(...)  → swift-frontend crash
     Trigger: AppearanceSettings.Controls.swift:107  `let onChange: @MainActor (Bool) -> Void`
     (Swift 6.3.2 / Xcode 26.5 toolchain crash on this @isolated(any) thunk; the project's
      verified runners differ — see apps/macos-pending-verifications.md.)

Both defects are in TeslaSync/{shared-surfaces,feature-views}; `git status` confirms this
unit modified only Localizable.xcstrings + TeslaSyncApp.swift and added 9 Admin/test files.
Per engineering guidelines ("Don't fix pre-existing issues unrelated to your task") these are
NOT modified here. The FeedbackQueue parity unit itself is COMPLETE and verified by every gate
that can run independently of the broken files (lint, format, placeholder, iOS+macOS typecheck,
executed model tests). The Shared.xcframework (KMP core) was built+staged successfully so the
blocker is purely the two source defects above, not a missing dependency / missing runner.

